        "body": "9. A: Melanie got straight As again this term.\nB: It doesn’t surprise me. She’s ____________________ student of all. (hard-working)\n      10. A: How was your holiday in the Caribbean?\nB: It was ____________________ trip I’ve ever taken. (relaxing)\n      11. A: I have to leave now. It’s getting late.\nB: Don’t go yet. Stay a bit ____________________ . (long)\n      12. A: Thanks for helping me clean up after the party.\nB: Don’t mention it. It’s ____________________ we could do. (little)\n      13. A: How much ____________________ is it to the airport? (far)\nB: About five minutes. Don’t worry. We’ll get there soon. \n      14. A: What did you think of Bob’s speech?\nB: It was OK, but Mary’s was much ____________________ . (interesting)\n      15. A: This place is too noisy. Can we go somewhere ____________________ ? (quiet)\nB: Yes, of course. \n      16. A: Did you have a nice time yesterday?\nB: Yes. The party was great. I stayed far ____________________ than I was expecting to. (long)\n      17. A: Do you like my homemade vegetarian lasagne?\nB: Yes, it’s ____________________ lasagne I’ve ever tasted. (good)\n      18. A: Did you enjoy Doug Thomson’s new adventure film?\nB: Yes, but his last film was much ____________________ . (exciting)\n      19. A: How do you like our new sofa?\nB: I love it. It’s ____________________ than your last one. (comfortable)\n      20. A: The Maths test was quite easy.\nB: I know. It was a lot ____________________ than I thought it would be. (easy)\n      21. A: Did you enjoy the Dragon roller coaster ride?\nB: Absolutely not! It was ____________________ ride I’ve ever been on. (frightening)\n      22. A: I think I’d prefer the brown dress.\nB: I know but this one is ____________________ . (cheap)",
